{"question": "How do I correct a rejected petty cash request?", "reversed": false, "sources": ["guide:cash_rejection:1", "guide:cash_rejection:0", "guide:cash_rejection:2"], "answer": "Rejection does not authorize release. Check the saved request state and pool before requesting again; a duplicate request is not the same as correcting a rejected one.\n\nIf cash is rejected or returned, open the recorded feedback, correct the purpose, amount or supporting information, then use the available revision or resubmission action.\n\nCancel or delete only in permitted states. Released advances, settlements and audit records follow the financial workflow rather than being erased to start again."}
{"question": "How do I correct a rejected petty cash request?", "reversed": true, "sources": ["guide:participation:1", "guide:participation:2"], "answer": "When updates are requested, correct and save the plan, then resend required approvals. A previous approval may not cover material changes to the revised plan.\n\nParticipation approval does not automatically publish a proposal, complete tasks or authorize cash. Inspect publication and financial checks separately."}
